                    {
                        "sense_id": "ce7944bf-e239-3523-96ae-ed871df67ec3",
                        "entry_id": "6c47e2e9-4174-3557-9c4d-68fe05d9b04c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Thirsty."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a700c6c8-5b11-4c98-afeb-56c8a43d28f7",
                                "sense_id": "ce7944bf-e239-3523-96ae-ed871df67ec3",
                                "text": "I will give unto him that is athirst of the fountain of the water of life freely."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2edade26-28a5-4c17-8182-ffc3c14fb5c2",
                                "sense_id": "ce7944bf-e239-3523-96ae-ed871df67ec3",
                                "text": "To this extenuated spectre, perhaps, a crumb is not thrown once a year; but when ahungered and athirst to famine—when all humanity has forgotten the dying tenant of a decaying house—Divine Mercy remembers the mourner, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c604d858-5212-4159-a488-ec321152146f",
                                "sense_id": "ce7944bf-e239-3523-96ae-ed871df67ec3",
                                "text": "Should you ever be athirst in the great American desert, try this experiment, if your caravan happen to be supplied with a metaphysical professor. Yes, as every one knows, meditation and water are wedded for ever."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0983cf03-edf8-327a-9502-5b417ae0b033",
                        "entry_id": "6c47e2e9-4174-3557-9c4d-68fe05d9b04c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Eager or extremely desirous (for something)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b34c640d-9660-43dd-a5e2-2d62b85eb4d0",
                                "sense_id": "0983cf03-edf8-327a-9502-5b417ae0b033",
                                "text": "I, that forever feel athirst for glory,\nCould at this moment be content to lie\nMeekly upon the grass, as those whose sobbings\nWere heard of none beside the mournful robins."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff9c23a7-c75f-488c-9b6c-5e940d157dff",
                                "sense_id": "0983cf03-edf8-327a-9502-5b417ae0b033",
                                "text": "O sleepless heart and sombre soul unsleeping,\nThat were athirst for sleep and no more life\nAnd no more love, for peace and no more strife!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c0a360d-1930-470d-ae27-64cce47e88ec",
                                "sense_id": "0983cf03-edf8-327a-9502-5b417ae0b033",
                                "text": "1913, Rabindranath Tagore, The Gardener, translated from the Bengali by the author, 5,\nI am restless. I am athirst for far-away things.\nMy soul goes out in a longing to touch the skirt of the dim distance."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
